   = note: `.mag()` takes a phasor, from `.at(f)`

error[E-measure]: `.db()` doesn't apply to a number, `V` (a voltage)
   --> measure_types.spl:17:33
   |
17 |     let volts_db = dc(output.v).db();
   |                                 ^^ a number, `V` (a voltage)
   |
   = note: `.db()` takes a phasor or a number with no unit

error[E-measure]: `.f_low()` doesn't apply to a number, `V` (a voltage)
   --> measure_types.spl:18:34
